The funnel converts 27 out of 150 users, resulting in an overall conversion rate of 18%, indicating inefficiency rather than lack of traffic.

Top-of-funnel performance is acceptable, but significant drop-offs begin after the Click stage.

The largest loss occurs between Qualified and Converted stages, making this the highest-impact area for optimization.

Email Nurture and Google Search are the most efficient channels, delivering higher conversion rates at lower cost.

LinkedIn B2B Outreach shows poor ROI due to high cost per conversion and lower success rates.

Conversion performance improves sharply in February but drops in March, showing inconsistency in campaign quality or audience mix.

Week-over-week metrics are highly volatile and less reliable; month-over-month trends provide a clearer performance signal.

Focusing on late-stage conversion and reallocating budget toward high-performing channels can significantly improve results without increasing spend.
